  "tagline": "Small-footprint embedded database with SQL and network-model APIs for RTOS, edge and safety-certified devices.",
  "description": "RaimaDB (long known as RDM, and before that db_VISTA) is an embedded database library for devices where SQLite is too heavy or not deterministic enough. It offers both SQL and a lower-level navigational (network model) API, in-memory or on-disk tables, and runs on RTOSes such as VxWorks, QNX and AUTOSAR Classic as well as Linux and Android. Raima sells a functional-safety certified edition with a sub-500 KB footprint and has shipped RaimaDB 16.1 (April 2026) with Python support and broader RTOS coverage. It is a specialist tool for avionics, telecom and industrial embedded systems.",
